<p><strong>Physiotherapy clinics in Nepal can keep a treatment course on schedule by booking follow-up sessions while the patient is still at the desk, tying each patient to a therapist, and recording part-payments across visits. Zennly schedules by therapist and room and tracks payments per booking.</strong></p>

<p>Physiotherapy is rarely one visit. Patients come back for a course of sessions, ideally with the same therapist, on a regular rhythm. If the schedule slips, so does recovery &ndash; and so does the clinic&rsquo;s income.</p>
<h2>Book the course, not just the next visit</h2>
<p>Booking one session at a time leaves gaps. Where possible, schedule the follow-ups while the patient is still at the front desk, with the same therapist, at times that suit them. Patients who leave with their next appointments already set are more likely to complete the course.</p>
<h2>Keep the therapist consistent</h2>
<p>Continuity matters to patients. A system that ties each patient&rsquo;s bookings to a therapist and shows that therapist&rsquo;s real availability makes continuity the default instead of an accident.</p>
<h2>Avoid double-bookings and idle gaps</h2>
<p>A clash wastes a treatment room and a patient&rsquo;s trip. An unfilled gap wastes the therapist&rsquo;s time. Seeing the whole day at a glance lets the front desk fill gaps and avoid clashes.</p>
<h2>Track payments across visits</h2>
<p>Because treatment happens over several visits, payments often come in parts. Record each payment against the booking so the clinic always knows what has been paid and what is outstanding.</p>
<h2>Give the owner visibility</h2>
<p>If the clinic has more than one branch, or more than one therapist, reports on revenue and staff performance make planning easier. <a href="/solutions/physiotherapy/">See how Zennly works for physiotherapy clinics</a>.</p>

<h2>Physiotherapy scheduling in Nepal: practical points</h2>
<p>Patients in Kathmandu Valley often travel some distance, so a missed or double-booked session costs more than an hour. Confirm the next appointments before the patient leaves, keep the same therapist where you can, and record each part-payment so the clinic always knows the outstanding balance.</p>

<h2>A clinic checklist for treatment courses</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Book the course, not just the first visit.</strong> Ask the patient to reserve the next sessions at the first appointment.</li>
<li><strong>Keep the same therapist</strong> where possible, and note a backup.</li>
<li><strong>Record attendance</strong> for each session so progress and missed visits are clear.</li>
<li><strong>Track payment per visit</strong> or per package, so balances are never guessed.</li>
<li><strong>Review weekly</strong> which courses are behind schedule and call those patients first.</li>
</ol>
